node.doctext:
If you need to do this in a module or a larger program, you can [local]ize the filehandle glob, or use the two-argument [select].  This is handy to avoid spooky action at a distance:
<code>open(OUT, ">firstout.txt") or die "1: $!\n";
print OUT "First\n";

{
    local *OUT;
    open(OUT, ">secondout.txt") or die "2: $!\n";
    print OUT "Second\n";
}

print OUT "Third\n";</code>
<p>
<strong>Update:</strong>  If there's an explicit [close], it's also worth checking for an error.  Someone on p5p had intermittent test failures (creating temporary files) on a nearly full disk.  I rarely check, but know I should.
